# Planted bugs for the ReBAC model. Each one must make the named check miss its expectation.
run fv-alloy rebac.als
properties NoUnintendedEditFromAncestorViewer_EditorChain NoUnintendedEditFromAncestorViewer_EditorOrViewerChain
file rebac.als

mutation the editor-chain rule also unions in viewer grants
detects NoUnintendedEditFromAncestorViewer_EditorChain
- fun editorsViaEditorChain[o: Object]: set User { o.*parent.editor }
+ fun editorsViaEditorChain[o: Object]: set User { o.*parent.editor + o.*parent.viewer }

mutation the editor-or-viewer-chain rule drops the viewer term it was meant to demonstrate
detects NoUnintendedEditFromAncestorViewer_EditorOrViewerChain
- fun editorsViaEditorOrViewerChain[o: Object]: set User { o.*parent.editor + o.*parent.viewer }
+ fun editorsViaEditorOrViewerChain[o: Object]: set User { o.*parent.editor }

harmless a comment on the parent field is reworded
- parent: lone Object,  -- the folder a document sits in, or none for a folder at the top
+ parent: lone Object,  -- the containing folder, or none for a top-level folder
